        <body>
            <div xml:id="d808">

                <pb facs="0883" n="797" xml:id="pg797"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bowen to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1902</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bowen reports that he has been authorized by the Venezuelan Government to
                    cable to the British and German consuls that they may return from Curacao to La
                    Guaira.</p>
                <p>Italy has presented a note which Venezuela interprets as similar to the British
                    and German notes.</p>
                <p>The minister for foreign affairs has just informed Mr. Bowen that President
                    Castro and his wife are going this afternoon to call on the German minister’s
                    wife.)</p>
            </div>
